  "id": "COMPOUND:31451 - PROTEIN:5943",
  "verbalization": "Propenyl propyl disulfide is implicated in the regulation of Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that this compound acts as a target for multiple compounds, including MIP, Tamarixinin B, and sec-Butyl acetate, all of which are known to interact with the same target protein. This indicates a potential mechanism of action involving the modulation of Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP, which is critical for cellular signaling and homeostasis. The presence of multiple targets pointing to the same protein suggests a possible role in the regulation of signaling pathways, possibly through the inhibition or activation of the enzyme. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP in maintaining cellular function, and the involvement of Propenyl propyl disulfide in this process may be mediated through its ability to influence the activity of this enzyme. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Propenyl propyl disulfide and the regulation of Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact mode of action.",
